    "created_at": "2017-04-23T15:34:08Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-23T15:34:08Z",
    "body": "The constructor needn't allow you to initialize anything.  It can take a plain EventInit dict, so it just lets you create it with no flags (beyond bubbles and cancelable, which you can set now with initEvent).\r\n\r\nYou can already fire a BeforeUnloadEvent in a beforeunload handler using createEvent(), in Chrome and Firefox.  This is consistent with the way the rest of the platform works.  Browsers already don't have to display the dialogs if they don't want to, so I think this can be left to a QoI issue, unless you have a specific concern that you think should be in the spec.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
